    "flow_gAVTzH": {
      "type": "flow",
      "blocks": {
        "media_NayzzC": {
          "type": "media",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/pexels-pavel-danilyuk-7108392.jpg",
            "show_sound_control": false,
            "video_url": "",
            "video_alt_text": "",
            "enable_video_autoplay": false,
            "subheading": "",
            "heading": "Measurement of Resting Metabolic Rate (RMR)",
            "image_style_heading": "square",
            "image_ratio_heading": "aspect-16/9",
            "description": "<p>The Aiwo RMR test measures the number of calories your body burns while at complete rest. This is done through a non-invasive breathing analysis that calculates how much oxygen you consume and carbon dioxide you produce while relaxed and at rest. RMR reflects your body's basic energy requirements to sustain vital functions such as breathing, circulation, and cell production, without accounting for any physical activity or movement.</p>",
            "button_text": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "open_new_window_button": false,
            "show_button_style": "text-link"
          }
        },
        "media_4VUdUM": {
          "type": "media",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/pexels-pavel-danilyuk-7108392.jpg",
            "show_sound_control": false,
            "video_url": "",
            "video_alt_text": "",
            "enable_video_autoplay": false,
            "subheading": "",
            "heading": "Basal Metabolic Rate (BMR) Calculation",
            "image_style_heading": "square",
            "image_ratio_heading": "aspect-16/9",
            "description": "<p>While RMR and BMR are closely related, BMR refers specifically to the energy expenditure under highly controlled conditions (e.g., after waking, in a fasted state, and complete rest), whereas RMR is measured in a typical relaxed resting state. Aiwo’s RMR testing can help estimate your BMR using well-established formulas, incorporating personal attributes like age, gender, height, and weight. This gives a baseline figure for the minimum number of calories your body needs to perform essential physiological functions.</p>",
            "button_text": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "open_new_window_button": false,
            "show_button_style": "text-link"
          }
        },
        "media_mHeMkm": {
          "type": "media",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/pexels-pavel-danilyuk-7108392.jpg",
            "show_sound_control": false,
            "video_url": "",
            "video_alt_text": "",
            "enable_video_autoplay": false,
            "subheading": "",
            "heading": "Assessment of Caloric Needs at Rest",
            "image_style_heading": "square",
            "image_ratio_heading": "aspect-16/9",
            "description": "<p>By accurately determining your RMR, the test reveals your individual caloric requirement for simply maintaining your body’s basic needs at rest. This value helps in understanding how many calories you would burn if you stayed at rest all day, which is critical for making informed decisions about calorie intake, weight management, and fitness planning.</p>",
            "button_text": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "open_new_window_button": false,
            "show_button_style": "text-link"
          }
        },
        "media_GKndj4": {
          "type": "media",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/pexels-pavel-danilyuk-7108392.jpg",
            "show_sound_control": false,
            "video_url": "",
            "video_alt_text": "",
            "enable_video_autoplay": false,
            "subheading": "",
            "heading": "Personalised Nutritional Recommendations",
            "image_style_heading": "square",
            "image_ratio_heading": "aspect-16/9",
            "description": "<p>After the test, Aiwo provides a personalized metabolism report, which is then reviewed by their expert team. You receive a consultation with an in-house doctor or nutritionist who interprets your RMR data to tailor bespoke dietary and lifestyle recommendations. This ensures your nutrition plan aligns precisely with your metabolism and health goals, helping you optimize your diet and achieve sustainable results.</p>",
            "button_text": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "open_new_window_button": false,
            "show_button_style": "text-link"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "media_NayzzC",
